      "writtenOn": "2026-11-17T02:00:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So there\u0027s three branches here where isWriteStarted is set to true:\n- quickCopy (line 712) -\u003e there\u0027s no read after this\n- small object (line 730) -\u003e no read after this either\n- large object (line 748) -\u003e this is the branch to inspect closer\n\nThe readFully on the second iteration might cause issues on line 742.\n\nBut right after starting the write, the header is immediately written:\n```\nisWriteStarted \u003d true;\nout.writeHeader(src, inflatedLength);\n```\n\nThere was no retrying in the old code either, regardless of a repack. There\u0027s also no real way of retrying either way, because the header is already written, we\u0027re locked into writing and we\u0027re expecting a fail because otp.getOffset() !\u003d out.length()\n\nI think the proposed code still works.\n\nreadFully just throws a plain EOFException so it would be hard to inspect the error deeper",
      "parentUuid": "7e0fe74d_687ebe2d",
      "revId": "b0862173d5932ccafdf0a3ec4a34c14e6d7fbc86",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
